xnu 0505: map the adsp pcm buffer through the audio smmu

The APM accepts both graphs and all three formats, but the PCM map was
refused because the buffer landed above 4 GiB and the map command carries
its address as `DDR tag | low 32 bits`. The live DT routes the ADSP audio
master through apps-SMMU stream 0x1801 (qcom,msm-audio-ion) and gives the
vendor's 0x10000000 IOVA pool, so the buffer can stay a high DDR
allocation: mondrian_audio_smmu.c programs a stage-1 context for SID
0x1801 with the context image and leaf attributes the Wi-Fi W2 proof
already exercised on this unit's apps-SMMU, maps the 16 KiB PCM buffer at
IOVA 0x10000000 and leaves the context enabled after the probe. The
worker maps and writes the period with the tagged IOVA and logs the
context FSR/GFSR after the DSP's write completion.
